<% content_for :title, "Publishing — Omarchy Plugins" %>
<section class="terminal-page">
  <article class="terminal-window terminal-window--ansi" aria-labelledby="publishing-title">
    <%= render "shared/terminal_window_header", title: "Publishing guide",
          route_alias: "publish.guide", status: "read only", command: "omarchy plugin publish --help", cursor: false %>

    <div class="terminal-window__layout">
      <nav class="terminal-window__index terminal-window__index--tree" aria-label="Publishing guide sections"
           data-controller="terminal-tree" data-terminal-tree-activate-last-at-bottom-value="true">
        <div class="terminal-window__index-inner">
          <b>Tree ./publishing</b>
          <div class="terminal-window__tree">
            <%= link_to "#quick-start", class: "is-active", aria: { current: "location" },
                  data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├─</span><span>quick start</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= link_to "#namespace", data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├─</span><span>namespace</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= link_to "#publish", data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├─</span><span>publish</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= link_to "#rules", data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├─</span><span>rules</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= link_to "#previews", data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">├─</span><span>previews</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= link_to "#trusted", data: { terminal_tree_target: "link", action: "terminal-tree#select" } do %>
              <span class="terminal-window__tree-branch" aria-hidden="true">└─</span><span>trusted</span>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </nav>

      <div class="terminal-window__main terminal-window__main--wide">
        <h1 id="publishing-title">Ship a plugin in minutes.</h1>
        <p class="terminal-window__lede">Push it anywhere — GitHub, Codeberg, your own Forgejo, or nowhere public at all. The registry never requires a forge. Tag, publish, done.</p>

        <section id="quick-start" class="terminal-section terminal-step" aria-labelledby="scaffold-title">
          <div class="terminal-step__number" aria-hidden="true">[1]</div>
          <div>
            <h2 id="scaffold-title" class="terminal-section__title">Scaffold</h2>
            <pre><code>$ omarchy plugin new weather</code></pre>
            <p>You get a <code>manifest.json</code>, a starter widget, a readme, and an optional CI publish workflow.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="namespace" class="terminal-section terminal-step" aria-labelledby="namespace-title">
          <div class="terminal-step__number" aria-hidden="true">[2]</div>
          <div>
            <h2 id="namespace-title" class="terminal-section__title">Claim your namespace</h2>
            <p><%= link_to "Sign in", new_session_path %> — no password; we email you a code — then claim your handle and enable two-factor authentication. Your plugin ID is <code>handle.name</code> and its install name is <code>handle/name</code>.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="publish" class="terminal-section terminal-step" aria-labelledby="publish-title">
          <div class="terminal-step__number" aria-hidden="true">[3]</div>
          <div>
            <h2 id="publish-title" class="terminal-section__title">Publish</h2>
            <pre><code>$ omarchy plugin publish
# device flow: approve the 8-char code in your browser, done.
# or, by hand:
$ tar czf weather-1.0.0.tar.gz manifest.json Widget.qml README.md
$ curl -X POST --data-binary @weather-1.0.0.tar.gz \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer omp_…" \
    https://plugins.omarchy.org/api/v1/plugins/you/weather/versions</code></pre>
            <p>A token from <code>omarchy plugin publish</code> is push-only, covers plugins in your namespaces, and expires in seven days. Trusted-publishing CI tokens are minted per plugin. Push-only tokens cannot yank, transfer ownership, or change account settings.</p>
            <p>Every version runs the same structural validation, malware scan, capability fingerprint, and hold before release. Versions are immutable: once <code>you/weather@1.0.0</code> exists, those bytes are frozen forever.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="rules" class="terminal-section" aria-labelledby="rules-title">
          <h2 id="rules-title" class="terminal-section__title"><span aria-hidden="true">$ </span>validate manifest</h2>
          <ul class="terminal-rules">
            <li><b>semver</b><span>Strict and always increasing. A used version remains burned even when rejected.</span></li>
            <li><b>license</b><span>An SPDX license is required. A repository is optional; trusted publishing links provenance to the exact commit.</span></li>
            <li><b>archive</b><span>No symlinks, no entry points outside the plugin directory, 10 MB maximum.</span></li>
            <li><b>identity</b><span>Manifest <code>id</code> must equal <code>yourhandle.pluginname</code>.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="previews" class="terminal-section" aria-labelledby="previews-title">
          <h2 id="previews-title" class="terminal-section__title">Make it look good</h2>
          <p>Ship one root screenshot named <code>preview.png</code>, <code>preview.jpg</code>, <code>preview.webp</code>, or <code>preview.gif</code>. It powers the directory card, click-to-zoom detail preview, and share card. Animated GIFs stay animated on the plugin page. Keep stills under 40 megapixels and recordings at 1440p or below; the registry generates optimized renditions.</p>
          <div class="terminal-status">
            <b>[ browse metadata ]</b>
            <p><code>category</code> accepts <% Registry::Taxonomy::CATEGORIES.each do |category| %><code><%= category %></code><%= " · " unless category == Registry::Taxonomy::CATEGORIES.last %><% end %>.</p>
            <p><code>tags</code> accepts up to <%= Registry::Taxonomy::MAX_TAGS %> entries from the curated vocabulary: <% Registry::Taxonomy::TAGS.each do |tag| %><code><%= tag %></code><%= ", " unless tag == Registry::Taxonomy::TAGS.last %><% end %>. Missing an obvious reusable tag? Request it in an issue; curation keeps filters meaningful.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="trusted" class="terminal-note terminal-note--wide">
          <h2>Prefer hands-off?</h2>
          <p>Register <b>trusted publishing</b> from your dashboard using repository, workflow, and environment. GitHub Actions is supported today. Tagging <code>v1.0.0</code> then publishes through OIDC with no stored secret and records provenance links to the exact commit and workflow run.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</section>
